`a fall of the risk, contract provides, request refused, notified` MEANS `A change in the insured risk` WITH
    `the factors the premium is based on changed so that the insured risk fell` IS TRUE
    `the factors the premium is based on changed so that the insured risk rose` IS FALSE
    `the contract provides for adjustment on such a change` IS TRUE
    `the insurer accepted the policyholder's request` IS FALSE
    `the policyholder accepted the insurer's request` IS FALSE
    `the terminating party notified the other immediately in writing` IS TRUE
`a fall of the risk, request refused, not notified` MEANS `A change in the insured risk` WITH
    `the factors the premium is based on changed so that the insured risk fell` IS TRUE
    `the factors the premium is based on changed so that the insured risk rose` IS FALSE
    `the contract provides for adjustment on such a change` IS TRUE
    `the insurer accepted the policyholder's request` IS FALSE
    `the policyholder accepted the insurer's request` IS FALSE
    `the terminating party notified the other immediately in writing` IS FALSE
`a fall of the risk, request accepted` MEANS `A change in the insured risk` WITH
    `the factors the premium is based on changed so that the insured risk fell` IS TRUE
    `the factors the premium is based on changed so that the insured risk rose` IS FALSE
    `the contract provides for adjustment on such a change` IS TRUE
    `the insurer accepted the policyholder's request` IS TRUE
    `the policyholder accepted the insurer's request` IS FALSE
    `the terminating party notified the other immediately in writing` IS TRUE
`a fall of the risk, contract silent` MEANS `A change in the insured risk` WITH
    `the factors the premium is based on changed so that the insured risk fell` IS TRUE
    `the factors the premium is based on changed so that the insured risk rose` IS FALSE
    `the contract provides for adjustment on such a change` IS FALSE
    `the insurer accepted the policyholder's request` IS FALSE
    `the policyholder accepted the insurer's request` IS FALSE
    `the terminating party notified the other immediately in writing` IS FALSE
`a rise of the risk, contract provides, refused by policyholder, notified` MEANS `A change in the insured risk` WITH
    `the factors the premium is based on changed so that the insured risk fell` IS FALSE
    `the factors the premium is based on changed so that the insured risk rose` IS TRUE
    `the contract provides for adjustment on such a change` IS TRUE
    `the insurer accepted the policyholder's request` IS FALSE
    `the policyholder accepted the insurer's request` IS FALSE
    `the terminating party notified the other immediately in writing` IS TRUE
`a rise of the risk, accepted by policyholder` MEANS `A change in the insured risk` WITH
    `the factors the premium is based on changed so that the insured risk fell` IS FALSE
    `the factors the premium is based on changed so that the insured risk rose` IS TRUE
    `the contract provides for adjustment on such a change` IS TRUE
    `the insurer accepted the policyholder's request` IS FALSE
    `the policyholder accepted the insurer's request` IS TRUE
    `the terminating party notified the other immediately in writing` IS TRUE
#ASSERT count (`Dieu 23(1): what the policyholder may ask for` `a fall of the risk, contract provides, request refused, notified`) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT null (`Dieu 23(1): what the policyholder may ask for` `a fall of the risk, contract silent`)
#ASSERT null (`Dieu 23(1): what the policyholder may ask for` `a rise of the risk, contract provides, refused by policyholder, notified`)
#ASSERT count (`Dieu 23(3): what the insurer may do` `a rise of the risk, contract provides, refused by policyholder, notified`) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `Dieu 23(2): the policyholder may terminate unilaterally` `a fall of the risk, contract provides, request refused, notified`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 23(2): the policyholder may terminate unilaterally` `a fall of the risk, request refused, not notified`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 23(2): the policyholder may terminate unilaterally` `a fall of the risk, request accepted`
#ASSERT `Dieu 23(4): the insurer may terminate unilaterally` `a rise of the risk, contract provides, refused by policyholder, notified`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 23(4): the insurer may terminate unilaterally` `a rise of the risk, accepted by policyholder`

